{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1520809-scion-titans-rising","id":1520809,"title":"Scion: Titans Rising","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-17T06:30:35-07:00","id":1520809,"title":"Scion: Titans Rising","content":"From Monday Meeting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coming up next for our crowd-funding: a two book set of <b>Scion: Titanomachy</b> and its sequel \u2013 <b>Scion: Titans Rising</b>! The campaign being designed to get both traditionally published books into your Friendly Local Game Stores! Expect that very late in August or very early in September.\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen any discussion on this, but awesome! What do we know about Titans Rising, if anything? Also, does this mean there is a possibility of the other Scion Books getting non POD releases (I haven't pulled the trigger yet as I would like the full line set to match)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T07:00:53-07:00","id":1520816,"title":"","content":"we know from the discord that there will be titans from all present pantheons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T18:18:37-07:00","id":1520851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordofIron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1520809-scion-titans-rising#post1520809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026 Also, does this mean there is a possibility of the other Scion Books getting non POD releases (I haven't pulled the trigger yet as I would like the full line set to match)</div> </div> </div> </div>Disclaimer: The following is opinion and speculation. Please do not take this anything more than me guessing at what will go into the decision making around titles currently in PDF/POD getting a shot at a future print run.<br /> <br /> I mean, anything is possible. My guess is it depends on the book. While I haven\u2019t read Titans Rising to be able to confirm this, I suspect there will be content which ties into Titanomachy. With the decision to crowd fund Titans Rising and have it available at your FLGS, it makes sense for to make Titanomachy available on the same store shelves next to it. Will other books currently available in PDF only get a traditional print run? It\u2019s going to depend on a few things.<br /> 1st relates to what I pointed out above. Titanomachy kinda goes with Titans Rising. Like I can see them being sold as a set in stores. Hell, I could picture a scenario like Mask of the Mythos where they added the supplement directly into the book (although it would probably be a bit awkward). Are there books currently available PDF only that match well enough with a title being crowd funded where it makes sense to sell them together (both during crowd funding and in retail)?<br /> 2nd is the printing process itself. I imagine there\u2019s a point where if a book is below a certain page count, the cost out printing out weighs the potential value of putting it out for retail sales. Titanomachy comes in around 160 pages in total. It\u2019s a couple pages longer than the smallest of the crowd funded books I own from OPP, so we know it\u2019s not in the too small to make sense to print. Are there other supplements out there long enough to make that cut? Like Saints &amp; Monsters is about 140, but if the cut off from the printer is 150 it could be just shy of the drop in production price.<br /> 3rd How well does this work? I\u2019m sure the folks over at OPP have stats and figures from previous crowd funding projects to get a decent idea of what they can expect out of new Scion sourcebook. What they don\u2019t know is how well an existing source book which is already in PDF, POD, and a platinum seller on DriveThru is going to do. This is a safe to test those waters. When the campaign is over they can sit back and look at how many folks chose to back for a physical copy of Titanomachy and use the data with other books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T10:26:33-07:00","id":1520896,"title":"","content":"My guess is that Titanomachy is the Titans from an external and often antagonistic perspective, Titans Rising is the Titans and their followers from their POV, and as potential allies to more conventional Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T20:40:08-07:00","id":1521161,"title":"","content":"According to the Monday Meeting Notes we\u2019ll find out soon. I look forward to seeing what folks think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T06:50:07-07:00","id":1521182,"title":"","content":"This is the first time I hope there is a delay with these crowdfunding projects. Things are a tad tight right now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T07:11:06-07:00","id":1521184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Playable Titans. Playable Titans, Playable Titans, <i>playable Titans</i>. Play them at any tier! Play them as heroes, monsters, or complicated, multifaceted individuals! Play them in the chapter of story hooks and tracks we\u2019ve provided, or weave them into your ongoing games. Give them new Callings, Birthrights and Knacks.<br /> <br /> Most of all, play them to finally call the Gods on their bullshit.<br /> \u2013 CAT EVANS\u200b </div> </div> </div>Why yes, that phone is ringing, and I'm on the other end...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T20:22:09-07:00","id":1521851,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/titans-rising-and-titanomachy-for-scion-2nd-edition-rpg?ref=activity\" target=\"_blank\">Just a reminder, it is live now</a>.<br /> <br /> Gotta say, the sample characters are interesting...I do find the draconic Heir that people think is a Titanic Scion pretty compelling. <br /> On the other hand, the fiction portrays the Karen character as significantly different than her playable write up does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T06:05:52-07:00","id":1522211,"title":"","content":"How are people liking the new Titans? From the first batch the K\u2019uh are my favorites, followed by the Balahala.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T14:53:09-07:00","id":1522237,"title":"","content":"As a practicing Buddhist, I'm curious to see what they do for the Palas. They already covered the obvious ones, Mara and his daughters, in <i>God</i>, and I'm not sure who else they can add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T11:20:49-07:00","id":1522278,"title":"","content":"Next stretch goal has been announced. The T-shirt is going to look bad ass!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T07:43:27-07:00","id":1523174,"title":"","content":"Lots of errata needed for the Relic section, I'm not sure if it was just because the dot ratings were missing a dot or two, or because they were missing the Demigod tag, but I did my best to note them all in the errata form.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, did anyone else think it odd to have a Catholic Saint who was born and raised in Jerusalem (St. Martha) be a Scion of a Greek/Roman goddess? Disregarding the fact that Saints are a thing in-setting (because Scion plays with them a bit differently than is strictly doctrinal), it's weird to have someone raised under Roman occupation be the recipient of power from a Greco-Roman divine figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}